  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Mole fraction is defined as the amount (number of moles or molecules) of a constituent or component divided by the total amount of all the constituent or component present. </p><p>Mole fraction<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Number</mi><mo> </mo><mi>of</mi><mo> </mo><mi>moles</mi><mo> </mo><mi>of</mi><mo> </mo><mi>compnent</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Total</mi><mo> </mo><mi>number</mi><mo> </mo><mi>of</mi><mo> </mo><mi>moles</mi><mo> </mo><mi>of</mi><mo> </mo><mi>all</mi><mo> </mo><mi>the</mi><mo> </mo><mi>components</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br/>Suppose we have a mixture with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> components A, B and C.</p><p>Mole fraction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, the answer is option B.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
